node_modules/
/node_modules
dist/
.expo/

# android/ is generated by `expo prebuild` at build time. A stale copy in the
# repository is a whole class of works-on-my-machine.
#
# ANCHORED for the same reason as /ios/ below: unanchored, this matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, so the day somebody adds an Android
# half to a local module under modules/, it would disappear from the
# repository without a word. Nothing here needs that, and the cost of the
# leading slash is nothing.
/android/
# ANCHORED. This was a bare `ios/`, which git matches against a directory of
# that name at ANY depth — so it silently swallowed
# modules/live-activity/ios/, the entire native half of the Live Activity.
# The JS and expo-module.config.json were committed, the Swift and the
# podspec were not, and autolinking would have gone looking for a module
# class that is not in the repository. Only the prebuild output at
# native/ios/ is meant to be ignored, so say so.
/ios/

# The repository root ignores package.json and package-lock.json outright —
# written when the web app had no npm dependencies at all and nothing here
# was ever meant to be installed. This app IS installed, and a build with no
# manifest and no lockfile is not a build. Deeper rules win, so these two
# come back.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
.darkshots/
ios-shots/

# Comparison renders. compare-all.mjs writes one directory per run — the
# default is .compare, and CMP_DIR puts it anywhere. 104MB of them were once
# committed by accident, which is 104MB in every clone for ever. They are
# evidence for a review, not source.
.compare/
cmp*/
final/
ios-shots/

# Raw captures for the App Store frames. The framed images in
# docs/store-assets/frames are the deliverable; these are the input, and
# store-web-shots.mjs regenerates them in a minute.
store-shots/

# Generated by scripts/widget-preview.mjs — pictures of a design, not the design.
widget-preview/
